Music","episode":"The History of Nerd Rock","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=h6snk0m4200"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":null,"body":"This album, released in 1989, is today considered a classic of Alt Rock. At the time, the band struggled to find an American label to release it, so they went through the British label 4AD, which specialized in experimental and avant-garde post-punk. \"Back then, they couldn't find anyone in America to release it so they had to go through 4AD, the British label which specialized in experimental and avant-garde post-punk.\"","year":1989,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The History of Alt-Rock: Chapter 11","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xdn31jMOOA4"}]}],"book_tracks":[{"id":250346004773319,"artist":"Pixies","artist_id":269588055362758,"title":"Doolittle","year":1989,"ess":1,"yt":"e5S9PgqQvE8","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Noise-rock y noise-pop","scene_id":32878711085175,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#noise-rock","chapters":["Sección 5.24"],"pages":[[1,218,null]]}],"others":[{"id":143040233182610,"type":"album","name":"Surfer Rosa","year":1988,"weight":47},{"id":236363655594674,"type":"album","name":"Bossanova","year":1990,"weight":25},{"id":113410353886943,"type":"song","name":"Debaser","year":1989,"weight":25},{"id":73677297176978,"type":"album","name":"Trompe Le Monde","year":1991,"weight":19},{"id":225187890224479,"type":"album","name":"Come On Pilgrim","year":1987,"weight":13},{"id":50033411385930,"type":"song","name":"Gigantic","year":1987,"weight":13},{"id":36196944998562,"type":"song","name":"Monkey Gone to Heaven","year":1989,"weight":13},{"id":272063665721284,"type":"song","name":"Wave of Mutilation (UK Surf Mix)","year":1989,"weight":7},{"id":139072907720798,"type":"album","name":"Indie Cindy","year":2014,"weight":7},{"id":7333007